\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O love, how deep, how broad, how high!
\par It fills the heart with ecstasy,
\par That God, the Son of God, should take
\par Our mortal form, for mortal's sake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He sent no angel to our race,
\par Of higher or of lower place,
\par But wore the robe of human frame
\par Himself, and to this lost world came.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For us He was baptized and bore
\par His holy fast, and hungered sore;
\par For us temptation sharp He knew;
\par For us the tempter overthrew.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For us He prayed, for us He taught,
\par For us His daily works He wrought:
\par By words and signs and actions thus
\par Still seeking, not Himself, but us.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For us to wicked men betrayed,
\par Scourged, mocked, in purple robe arrayed,
\par He bore the shameful Cross and death, 
\par For us at length gave up His breath.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. For us He rose from death again,
\par For us He went on high to reign;
\par For us He sent His Spirit here
\par To guide, to strengthen, and to cheer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. To Him whose boundless love has won
\par Salvation for us through His Son,
\par To God the Father, glory be,
\par Both now and through eternity.
\par                                          Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

